.TH which 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
which \- show which file a command name runs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B which
.I "command ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
For each
.IR command ,
.B which
searches
.B PATH
and prints the full path of the first executable file of that name.
.PP
If
.B PATH
is not set,
.B /bin
is searched.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if every name was found, 1 otherwise.  A name that is not found
produces no output at all, only the status.
.SH NOTES
.B which
knows nothing about the shell built-ins, so it will not tell you that
.B cd
is one.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR printenv (1)
